@ 8.5 - Proto-Altaic to Proto-Turkic
# citation: Pogostick Man, from Wikipedia contributors (2011), “Altaic languages”. Wikipedia, the Free Encyclopedia. NB: Does not include clusters. Loss of syllable pitch The wiki at Firespeaker.org gives the following alternate list of sound changes from Proto-Altaic to (Pre-)Proto-Turkic. Pogostick Man, from Firespeaker.org wiki contributors (2014), “Turkic sound changes”.
	{ a, ø } > { {a,ʌ}, a } / P_Ca
	{ a, e, i, u, æ, ø, y } > { a, {a,ʌ,e}, {ɯ,i}, {u,o}, {ia,ja,ɛ}, {ia,ja}, ɯ } / _Ca
	y > i / :{ rʲ_e, lʲ_e }:
	e > ja / #_C{e,i}
	ø > ʌ / P_Ce
	i > e / :{ rʲ_e, lʲ_e }:
	{ a, {e,i}, o, u, æ, ø, y } > { {ɛ,a}, ɛ, {ø,o}, {y,u}, {ia,ja,ɛ}, {ia,ja}, {y,ø} } / _Ci
	æ > a / P_Co
	æ > ʌ / P_Cu
	{ a, e, i, æ, ø, y } > { {o,ja,aj}, {ʌ,ɜ}, ɯ, {ia,ja}, {o,u}, {u,o} } / _Co
	{ e, i, æ, ø, y } > { {ɛ,a,ʌ}, {ɯ,i}, {e,a}, {u,o}, ɯ } / _Cu
	{pʰ,ŋ} > {∅,j} / #_
	pʰ > p
	tʰ > d / #_(V){lʲ,rʲ}
	tʰ > t
	{t,t͡ʃ} > d / #_
	k > ɡ / _(V)r
	kʰ > k
	ʃ > t͡ʃ / #_a
	ʃ > s
	{ m, nʲ } > { b, j } / #_
	{ʒ,d͡ʒ} > j / #_ (marked as to Pre-Proto-P:[-voice]urkic)
	{d,n} > j / #_ (?) (marked as to Pre-Proto-P:[-voice]urkic)
	{N,l,r,ʃ,z} > ∅ / #_
	p > ɸ / #_
	ɸ > h / #_
	d ɡ > t k (may have been part of a more sweeping merger; Firespeaker calls it “lenis-fortis”)
	{ dʲ, nʲ } sʲ > j ʃ / #_
	rʲ > z